What is here
------------
src/lower_mac/  crc_simple.[ch], tetra_conv_enc.[ch], tetra_interleave.[ch],
                tetra_rm3014.[ch], tetra_scramb.[ch], tch_reordering.c
src/phy/        tetra_burst.[ch]
src/            tetra_common.[ch], tetra_mac_pdu.[ch], tetra_llc_pdu.[ch],
                tetra_mle_pdu.[ch], tetra_mm_pdu.[ch], tetra_cmce_pdu.[ch],
                tetra_sndcp_pdu.[ch], tetra_tdma.h
compat/osmocom/core/utils.h
                NOT from libosmocore: a stand-in written for this component
                with the few helpers the files above use (value_string lookup,
                ARRAY_SIZE). No libosmocore code is vendored.

Not vendored (replaced by code in ../../src, written for this component):
the demodulator (GNU Radio flow graphs, float_to_bits), tetra_burst_sync.c,
the Viterbi decoders (viterbi*.c, libosmocore conv), tetra_lower_mac.c,
tetra_upper_mac.c, tetra_llc.c (msgb/talloc reassembly), tetra_tdma.c, the
crypto/ directory, tetra_gsmtap.c, the codec/ directory and all programs.

Changes to the vendored files
-----------------------------
Unmodified: crc_simple.[ch], tetra_conv_enc.h, tetra_interleave.h,
tetra_scramb.[ch], tetra_cmce_pdu.[ch], tetra_mac_pdu.h, tetra_mle_pdu.h,
tetra_mm_pdu.h, tetra_sndcp_pdu.h, tetra_tdma.h.

lower_mac/tch_reordering.c
  - class0_positions[]: third entry of the row "41, 42, 33" corrected to 43
    (33 appeared twice), and the missing last entry 64 added (the table had
    50 of its 51 entries). Both follow EN 300 395-2 table 4 and make the
    type-1 -> codec bit mapping a bijection (checked in host/test_unit.c).
lower_mac/tetra_conv_enc.c
  - dump_state() only compiled with DEBUG (it is only used by DEBUGP).
  - signed/unsigned comparison fixes (-Wextra).
  - the puncturer self test (test_one_punct, tetra_punct_test: printf, malloc)
    is only compiled with TETRA_CONV_ENC_SELFTEST.
lower_mac/tetra_interleave.c
  - loop counters made uint32_t (-Wextra sign comparison).
lower_mac/tetra_rm3014.c / .h
  - printf of the generator matrix rows in tetra_rm3014_init() removed.
  - prototype typo tetra_rm3013_decode -> tetra_rm3014_decode.
phy/tetra_burst.c / .h
  - phase2bits[]: entries for -1 and +3 were swapped relative to bits2phase[]
    and EN 300 392-2 table 5.1; the table was indexed without the PHASE()
    offset (out of bounds for negative phase adjustments). Fixed; this only
    affects the phase adjustment bits of the burst builders (used by the test
    signal generator), not reception.
  - printf in sum_up_phase() removed; sum_up_phase() exported.
  - unused uplink / 3-bit-per-symbol tables put under #if 0; (size_t) casts
    and (void) len for -Wextra.
  - added tetra_burst_train_seq_bits() and tetra_burst_freq_corr_bits():
    read-only access to the training sequence tables for the soft-decision
    burst synchroniser in ../../src/tetra_modem.c.
  - tetra_burst_rx_cb() (upstream code, it splits one burst into its blocks
    and calls tp_sap_udata_ind()) is declared in the header; it is called
    with int8 soft bits instead of hard bits and tp_sap_udata_ind() is
    implemented in ../../src/tetra_lmac.c.
tetra_common.c / .h
  - struct tetra_phy_state, struct tetra_mac_state, the global t_phy_state,
    tetra_mac_state_init() and tetra_get_sap_name() removed (all receiver
    state is per instance in ../../src/tetra_ctx.h); includes of
    linuxlist.h, bits.h and tetra_prim.h removed.
  - duplex spacing made int32_t (the table holds negative values).
tetra_llc_pdu.c / .h
  - printf("WARNING llc pdu too small ...") removed (the caller gets the
    error through the parsed structure).
  - loop counter type; llist/msgb based struct tllc_state and
    struct tllc_defrag_q_e removed.
tetra_mac_pdu.c
  - tetra_addr_dump() (sprintf into a static buffer) is only compiled with
    TETRA_ADDR_DUMP; its %u arguments are cast for targets where uint32_t is
    unsigned long.
tetra_mle_pdu.c, tetra_mm_pdu.c, tetra_sndcp_pdu.c
  - "(void) uplink;" for -Wextra.

With these changes the vendored files reference no stdio function, do not
allocate, and keep no state between calls apart from two constant tables
filled in on first use: rm_30_14_rows[] (tetra_rm3014_init(), called from
tetra_rx_create()) and tsq_bytes[] in tetra_find_train_seq() (hard-decision
training sequence search; not called by the library).
